  "articleBody": "Deciding when to tackle under cabinet lighting yourself and when to call in a pro can be a bit tricky, but here are some clear signals. You definitely want to bring in a professional if: \n*   **You're dealing with new wiring.** If you need to run new lines through walls or add outlets, that's firmly in licensed electrician territory. \n*   **It's a hardwired installation.** While plug-in options are DIY-friendly, hardwired systems connect directly to your home's electrical system, which can be complex and requires specific expertise to do safely and up to code. \n*   **You're uncomfortable with your home's electrical system.** If working with wires or circuit panels makes you nervous, trust your gut. Safety first! \n*   **You're troubleshooting existing wiring issues.** If your current electrical system isn't cooperating, a pro can diagnose and fix underlying problems. \n\nFor any of these situations, bringing in experienced help, like Abraham and the team at HH Remodeling LLC, ensures the job is done safely, efficiently, and correctly, avoiding potential hazards and ensuring your beautiful new lighting works perfectly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
